From 85137b87ab1f5b1e63ef06048265b72977adb4f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 17:01:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): Heidenhain DIN/ISO writes the G62 filter mode and
 checks the T range

heidenhain.cps writes G62 T<tol> P01 <0 finish|1 rough> P02 0 where the
control profile takes P01. Two new resolver flags (g62_mode, g62_t_max_um)
carry the documented word and the largest T for each control and NC
software. A T above the range, a T that rounds to T0, and smoothing on a
control without cycle 32 are refused by name. The Picomax 55 (iTNC 530
340490-03, option 2 not listed) keeps its G62 T-only output.

Fixes #4226

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
